{
  "$comment": "How a session's row reads on the sessions page (ADR 0029): who it is, its mode and model, a status chip for uncommon states, when, and a detail under it. `now` is 2026-10-02T14:00:00Z; `ago` is minutes before now and `next_in` minutes after it. `row` names the session whose row is checked among `sessions`; `task_title` is the page's task (empty on the project's brainstorm page). `report` is a message the delegate sent, and `messages_loaded` says the task's messages have loaded: the server never has them, so view_test.go skips the cases where it is true, and the browser's view.test.js reads all. `unsandboxedAttr` is the attribute value x-bind sets: \"\" for an unsandboxed row, null for any other. Read by web/src/modules/sessions/presentation/view.test.js and internal/adapter/in/web/sessions/view_test.go.",
